t value since 2010 registered in 2021 (i.e. 33 casualties).   \nFigure 8 - Railway \"internal\" and \"external\" significant accidents (EU-27, 2010-2021)\n---\n=== Page 11 has suicide ===\n EUROPEAN UNION AGENCY FOR RAILWAYS                                                                                                                     Safety Overview 2023\n \n \n \n120 Rue Marc Lefrancq  |  BP 20392  |  FR-59307 Valenciennes Cedex \n11 / 15 \nTel. +33 (0)327 09 65 00  |  era.europa.eu \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \nFigure 11 - Railway suicides and trespasser fatalities (EU-27, 2007-2021)\nSource: Common Safety Indicators (CSIs) as reported by National Safety Authorities (NSAs) to the Agency\n2007\n2008\n2009\n2010\n2011\n2012\n2013\n2014\n2015\n2016\n2017\n2018\n2019\n2020\n2021\nSuicides\n2417\n2211\n2552\n2532\n2687\n2734\n2552\n2608\n2511\n2608\n2532\n2379\n2313\n2204\n2234\nTrespasser fatalities\n822\n887\n813\n750\n759\n622\n659\n692\n572\n585\n579\n549\n491\n411\n405\n0\n500\n1000\n1500\n2000\n2500\n3000\nFigure 12 - Railway employee casualties (EU-27, 2010-2021)\nFatalities, serious injuries\nSource: Common Safety Indicators (CSIs) as reported by National Safety Authorities (NSAs) to the Agency\n2010\n2011\n2012\n2013\n2014\n2015\n2016\n2017\n2018\n2019\n2020\n2021\nSeriously injured\n90\n76\n81\n71\n62\n47\n49\n64\n57\n40\n44\n33\nKilled\n44\n30\n45\n28\n28\n34\n33\n26\n24\n12\n31\n25\n0\n20\n40\n60\n80\n100\n120\n140\n160\nNumber of employee fatalities and serious injuries\n\n---", "cwd": "/tmp/pinchbench/a26a2fd5/agent_workspace"}, "isError": false, "timestamp": 1775590210331}}
